   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "From a hundred to a million",
     "texto": [
      "The number 100 on its own or before a noun is **cien**: **cien euros**. From 101 to 199 use **ciento**: **ciento uno**, **ciento veinte**.\n\nThe hundreds are **one word** and agree with the noun: **doscientos**, trescientos, cuatrocientos, **quinientos**, seiscientos, **setecientos**, ochocientos, **novecientos**. Doscient**as** páginas.\n\n**Y** only goes between tens and units: ciento treinta **y** cinco. Never «ciento y cinco».\n\n**Mil** does not change: **dos mil**, **tres mil**. Years are read as ordinary numbers: 2025 is **dos mil veinticinco**.\n\n**Un millón** takes **de** before a noun: **un millón de euros**, **tres millones de habitantes**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Hundreds, thousands and ordinals",
     "texto": [
      "Rules worth remembering:\n\n- **cien** on its own or before a noun; **ciento** when another number follows: **ciento cinco**.\n- The hundreds agree in gender: **doscientos euros**, **doscientas personas**.\n- **quinientos**, **setecientos** and **novecientos** are irregular.\n- **mil** does not change: **dos mil euros**.\n- **primero** and **tercero** shorten before a masculine noun: **el primer piso**, **el tercer día**. **Segundo** does not shorten.\n\nIn Spain decimals use a comma and thousands are separated with a space: **1 000 000**."
     ],
